{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require convicted domestic abuse offenders to be placed on a national register",
        "additional_details": "We believe a register could support risk management, improve information sharing, and help prevent further abuse.\r\n\r\nAs someone who has experienced domestic abuse in both my childhood and adulthood, and who knows many other women who have experienced it too, I feel strongly that there should be a register to help protect potential future partners from repeat offenders. I believe greater transparency and appropriate information sharing could help prevent further abuse and improve public safety.",
        "background": "Create a national register for people convicted of domestic abuse offences, with appropriate safeguards, to help protect future partners and improve public safety. Domestic abuse often involves repeat offending. ",
